														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2460905">
									

<p>I kind of want to like this, but it's just not quite doing it. It's well done technically, and the interviews and Document 2291-A almost have me upvoting (the imagery in the latter has a nice creep factor). What its missing is that impossible-to-define &quot;something&quot; that pushes a work from &quot;not bad&quot; to &quot;interesting&quot;.</p>
<p>Two questions/suggestions that might spark some brainstorming: &quot;Why fun, and not any other word?&quot; and &quot;Assume that this <em>wasn't</em> created to exploit employees. What else could have been the intent, and was this the intended outcome?&quot;.</p>
<p>Edit: after some consideration, upvoted.</p>

