			<div class="content" id="post-content-2665310">
									

<p>I like it. The idea is interesting to me, just a couple of technical issues I see.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Suggested&nbsp;edits</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Suggested&nbsp;edits</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The following interview has been deemed notable due to its content.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence suggests a single interview log; however, there are two interview logs that follow.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>D-14683, a former paralegal, was chosen for testing with SCP-2291. To test the long-term effects of SCP-2291 on subjects similar to the employees of █████████ Corporate Solutions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These two sentences should be one. The second sentence feels weird reading, and from context clues, appears to be an incomplete sentence. The question &quot;What is used to test long term effects&#8230;&quot; should be answered here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He found dead in his cell 4 months and 12 days after the above interview.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should be &quot;He <em>was</em> found dead&#8230;&quot;.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Keep up the good work!</p>

